The attached image is Figure 1 from the npj Vaccines (2017) paper. It is a box-and-whisker plot illustrating anti-rPA IgG antibody titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with various doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11. The data shows that Nano-11 significantly boosts rPA-specific IgG titers, achieving comparable immunopotentiation to AH at higher doses (200 and 50 µg). Importantly, Nano-11 at a lower dose (12.5 µg) still elicited a strong antibody response, outperforming AH at the same concentration, highlighting its superior adjuvant efficacy at low doses.